Step 1 — Bijection: codons ↔ blades of Cl(6,0)
A codon is 6 bits, i.e. a subset S ⊆ {1,…,6}; the algebra's canonical basis
is {e_S : S ⊆ {1,…,6}}. The map codon ↦ e_S is a bijection of 64-element
sets, and it is multiplicative: the blade of a codon is the product of the
three nucleotide blades (disjoint generator sets commute up to sign).
Product table: e_S e_T = σ(S,T) e_{S△T}, σ = (−1)^{inv(S,T)}.
